diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 34d28918..3d3ff594 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -193,2 +193,4 @@ DM_PATCH_FRONT	switch	`=<bytes>`: the size of the patch area right before the mo
 DM_PHONE_MOTION	switch	On iOS, whether the phone's own device motion drives player 1's six-axis sensor: `auto` (default) while no controller supplies fresh motion, `1` phone only, `0` never; each source keeps its own orientation
+DM_PHONE_ROTATE	player	On iOS, `auto` (default; on iOS 27 and later none, since Core Motion delivers the samples in the picture's frame; on iOS 26 one quarter turn more on a known foldable's inner screen (recognized by its shape), in every orientation) or `<0..3>` (launcher setting **Gyro rotation**) turns the phone's gyro that many more quarter turns about the screen's normal, for a screen that sits turned against the phone's body (a foldable's inner screen)
+DM_PORTRAIT_LAYOUT	player	On iOS, `0` turns off the portrait layout (default on; launcher setting **iPhone Duo portrait: game above the controls**): only on the iPhone Duo's inner screen held upright (every other iPhone and iPad stays landscape and is not affected), the picture is shown at the top of the screen and the on-screen controls are laid out below it (`DmGamepad.m`, `mtl_set_present_top`), instead of the picture centred with the controls over the whole screen
 DM_PREEMPT	switch	`0` / `1` overrides the profile's `core_preempt`: also check already-runnable higher-priority peers on the caller's core after every thread SVC
diff --git a/docs/frontends.md b/docs/frontends.md
index 97eda507..e6842b61 100644
--- a/docs/frontends.md
+++ b/docs/frontends.md
@@ -44,2 +44,3 @@ A built app carries the settings its game supports, as the iPhone app's settings
 - `needs` (optional): `<VAR>=<value>` makes the row a sub-setting of the row that sets `<VAR>`, drawn only while that row has that value (Rumble strength only while rumble is on). A row naming a variable the list does not have stays drawn.
+- `device` (optional): `foldable` marks a setting only an iPhone Duo can use (its inner screen's portrait layout). The iPhone app draws it only on a Duo (recognized by its inner screen's shape, and remembered once the game has run there, so the closed screen shows it too); a front end that cannot tell the device may leave it out, or draw it, where it does nothing.
 - An app without the file has no settings to offer: start it as it is.
